WEBVTT

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:09.320
Last lesson. I promised you a second
brain.

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:13.620
I wasn't joking. Everything on this screen
was done by one worker.

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:15.780
It doesn't sleep. It doesn't get tired.

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:20.120
It has never once said, "That's not my
job." It already works for you.

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:22.780
It's been sitting there this whole time,
waiting.

00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:24.880
Today, you give it a real job.

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:28.880
And later, I'll show you one line almost
nobody thinks to type.

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:31.240
It's the most useful trick in this lesson.

00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:33.680
Hi, I'm Adil. Welcome back.

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:38.180
Today, we get to the most important tool
in this course, your second brain.

00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:42.360
Think of it as an employee you can bring
almost any digital task to.

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:46.450
You'll use it for a task from your
everyday life and a scene from your own

00:00:46.580 --> 00:00:51.840
imagination. I'll show you each step, and
neither of us will write the video

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:56.100
prompt. To do that, on the Higgsfield
homepage, click Supercomputer in the

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:58.800
top menu. It opens in a new tab.

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:02.920
You met this tool last lesson when it
helped turn our first idea into a

00:01:02.920 --> 00:01:07.050
video prompt. This empty box is where we
give it the next

00:01:07.060 --> 00:01:08.490
job.

00:01:09.560 --> 00:01:12.320
LLM stands for Large Language Model.

00:01:12.320 --> 00:01:16.220
During training, it learns patterns from
huge amounts of text that lets it

00:01:16.220 --> 00:01:21.020
explain a difficult subject, write a
script, plan a project, or write code.

00:01:21.020 --> 00:01:23.560
You describe the job in ordinary language.

00:01:23.560 --> 00:01:27.020
You've probably heard of ChatGPT, Claude,
and Gemini.

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:29.360
Those assistants use language models.

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:32.780
Different models have different strengths,
some are faster, others are built

00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:36.280
for more complex work. Think of the LLM as
the brain.

00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:40.100
Supercomputer gives it a desk and tools so
it can look things up online and

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:41.960
work with video generation.

00:01:41.960 --> 00:01:46.920
Next, click Auto under the box to choose
which language model we'll talk

00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:49.240
to. Auto is already selected.

00:01:49.240 --> 00:01:52.400
I'll leave it there, and close the menu by
clicking outside it.

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:55.900
Think of it as the smartest intern on
Earth on day one.

00:01:55.900 --> 00:01:59.140
It may know your name. That doesn't mean
it knows what you need to get done

00:01:59.140 --> 00:02:01.280
by Friday and how it can help you.

00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:03.680
So give it a brief. Who are you?

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:06.100
What do you need? What should it do?

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:07.900
What should the answer look like?

00:02:07.900 --> 00:02:11.040
That's context. What it needs to know
about your task.

00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:15.060
It can include your notes, a brief, a
spreadsheet, images, or a reference

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:19.000
video. Whatever is useful in a format your
tool can read.

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:20.660
Four parts of the context.

00:02:20.660 --> 00:02:25.900
I am, I need, do, format. You don't have
to type the labels,

00:02:25.900 --> 00:02:29.680
just include the information.

00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:33.200
I need to choose AI news for my YouTube
channel this week.

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:35.520
Let's see what our new employee makes of
this.

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:40.340
In the message box, I type find me AI
news, then click the send

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:43.760
arrow. Let's see what it brings back.

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:48.780
Okay, it gave me a roundup for this week
with sources.

00:02:48.780 --> 00:02:53.940
That's a useful start. But I never put
this week in the message and I

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:57.300
haven't told it who watches my channel or
what I'm going to do with the

00:02:57.300 --> 00:03:00.400
news. It had to make those choices for me.

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:02.820
Let's tell the intern what this list is
for.

00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:04.860
One habit before we try again.

00:03:04.860 --> 00:03:07.200
Keep each job in its own chat.

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:10.920
Your shopping list doesn't need a
supporting role in your space movie.

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:14.660
Same job, same chat. New job, new chat.

00:03:14.660 --> 00:03:16.860
Normally I'd add the missing details right
here.

00:03:16.860 --> 00:03:19.940
I'm opening a fresh chat only to compare
the two briefs.

00:03:19.940 --> 00:03:22.820
Watch me give that intern an actual brief.

00:03:22.820 --> 00:03:26.060
I make YouTube videos about generative AI.

00:03:26.060 --> 00:03:30.540
Research the most important AI news from
the last few days and rank it most

00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:35.020
trending first. For each item, one line on
why my audience would

00:03:35.020 --> 00:03:38.360
care. Now I click the send arrow.

00:03:38.360 --> 00:03:42.660
There we go. The news is ranked and each
story comes with a reason my

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:46.440
audience would care. That's a useful first
day on the job.

00:03:46.440 --> 00:03:50.860
From this shortlist, I can choose a story,
ask for three script versions,

00:03:50.860 --> 00:03:54.060
then use supercomputer to generate clips
for the edit.

00:03:54.060 --> 00:03:58.540
Same project, same chat. And a news list
is a small job.

00:03:58.540 --> 00:04:03.440
Give a coding capable LLM research and
references and it can help write the

00:04:03.440 --> 00:04:08.120
code for an interactive 3D scene like an
engine that assembles itself then

00:04:08.120 --> 00:04:10.660
shows its moving parts in action.

00:04:10.660 --> 00:04:12.150
You still need to test the result

00:04:12.980 --> 00:04:15.400
but the starting point is the same.

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:19.040
Explain what you want to make and give it
the material it needs.

00:04:19.040 --> 00:04:24.220
You can use those four parts for a
customer message, a packing list or a

00:04:24.220 --> 00:04:29.100
plan for tomorrow. Pause here and try it
with a task you actually need done

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:34.440
this week. Open a new chat and use the
four parts on screen to explain the

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:37.540
job. Read the answer against the job you
gave it.

00:04:37.540 --> 00:04:41.400
Does it include the details you need in a
form you can use?

00:04:41.400 --> 00:04:43.420
Check any facts you'll rely on.

00:04:43.420 --> 00:04:47.120
If something important is missing, add
that detail in the same

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:52.520
chat. I used to work as a bartender and
this idea came to me

00:04:52.520 --> 00:04:54.590
while I was working.

00:04:55.420 --> 00:04:57.860
Let's give our employee that scene.

00:04:57.860 --> 00:05:01.800
Here's all I'm bringing. A bartender
closes his empty bar at three in the

00:05:01.800 --> 00:05:05.740
morning. He switches the lights off one by
one and when he kills the last

00:05:05.740 --> 00:05:09.460
light, he walks slowly to the big window
and stands there.

00:05:09.460 --> 00:05:12.520
Sad and tired, looking far into the
distance.

00:05:12.520 --> 00:05:16.200
Outside the window, far away in the dark,
hangs the earth.

00:05:16.200 --> 00:05:19.260
His bar is in space. Three sentences.

00:05:19.260 --> 00:05:24.360
Who, where, what happens? Nothing about
lenses or camera angles, just a

00:05:24.360 --> 00:05:28.920
scene I want to see. I want to be the
bartender so I'll attach my photo.

00:05:28.920 --> 00:05:31.760
Now, I could just say, write me a prompt.

00:05:31.760 --> 00:05:34.160
But how would it know what I have in mind?

00:05:34.160 --> 00:05:35.940
Here's the line I promised you.

00:05:35.940 --> 00:05:39.260
Before it writes the prompt, make it
interview you.

00:05:39.260 --> 00:05:43.340
Ask it to ask you. A good question can
make you notice a choice you haven't

00:05:43.340 --> 00:05:46.580
made yet. Warm wood or cold metal?

00:05:46.580 --> 00:05:50.800
Lonely or frightened? If it starts
drafting straight away, send another

00:05:50.800 --> 00:05:52.660
message asking for the questions first.

00:05:52.660 --> 00:05:56.180
It's a new job, so I click new chat in the
sidebar.

00:05:56.180 --> 00:06:00.500
Under the box, open ask mode and check ask
before generating.

00:06:00.500 --> 00:06:03.660
I want to approve the request before
anything is generated.

00:06:03.660 --> 00:06:06.560
The creative questions go in the message
itself.

00:06:06.560 --> 00:06:11.200
For the photo, click the plus beside the
message box, then attach file.

00:06:11.200 --> 00:06:14.640
In assets, click upload media and choose
your photo.

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:18.560
Wait until its thumbnail appears beside
the message, then type the idea and

00:06:18.560 --> 00:06:20.820
tell it to use the person in that photo.

00:06:20.820 --> 00:06:24.700
Underneath, I add, before you write the
video prompt, ask me the questions

00:06:24.700 --> 00:06:26.840
you need answered to make this great.

00:06:26.840 --> 00:06:29.680
Write the prompt only after I've answered.

00:06:29.680 --> 00:06:31.340
Now, click the send arrow.

00:06:31.340 --> 00:06:33.040
Let's see what it needs to know.

00:06:33.040 --> 00:06:37.700
As you answer, think about what we should
see, hear, and feel.

00:06:37.700 --> 00:06:40.640
For the frame, I click 16 by 9.

00:06:40.640 --> 00:06:43.360
For the length, I click 15 seconds.

00:06:43.360 --> 00:06:45.920
Each choice takes me straight to the next
question.

00:06:45.920 --> 00:06:48.300
Next, it asks what the bar should feel
like.

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:51.260
I choose something else and type
realistic.

00:06:51.260 --> 00:06:55.420
A warm wooden bar with normal gravity, not
a neon sci-fi set.

00:06:55.420 --> 00:06:58.540
Then I click continue. Now the camera.

00:06:58.540 --> 00:07:02.940
I choose something else and type one
continuous slow camera move towards the

00:07:02.940 --> 00:07:05.740
window. Keep the window outside the
opening frame.

00:07:05.740 --> 00:07:09.280
Reveal the earth only when he reaches the
window at the end.

00:07:09.280 --> 00:07:14.140
Then I click continue. For sound, I click
diegetic sounds only, no music.

00:07:14.140 --> 00:07:16.340
That sends all five answers.

00:07:16.340 --> 00:07:19.740
Here's the summary. I check that it kept
the choices I made.

00:07:19.740 --> 00:07:21.380
Your questions may be different.

00:07:21.380 --> 00:07:24.820
Pick the answers that fit your idea and
add anything important it missed.

00:07:24.820 --> 00:07:26.840
There's the prompt. I didn't write it.

00:07:26.840 --> 00:07:30.100
I answered questions. Let's see whether
our employee listened.

00:07:30.100 --> 00:07:33.620
Hang on. It starts with just the last
light.

00:07:33.620 --> 00:07:36.120
I wanted him to switch them off one by
one.

00:07:36.120 --> 00:07:38.140
Here's the note I sent in the same chat.

00:07:38.140 --> 00:07:42.120
Show him switching several lights off one
by one before the slow walk to the

00:07:42.120 --> 00:07:45.260
window. Now I scroll to the revision.

00:07:45.260 --> 00:07:47.900
There. The lights go off in sequence.

00:07:47.900 --> 00:07:49.860
Now the instructions match the scene.

00:07:49.860 --> 00:07:53.980
If it adds or changes something you don't
want, fix the text first.

00:07:53.980 --> 00:07:55.960
Ask about any unclear line.

00:07:55.960 --> 00:07:58.640
The prompt should still describe your
idea.

00:07:58.640 --> 00:08:01.700
Remember lesson one. A generation is a
take.

00:08:01.700 --> 00:08:04.880
This one's a rehearsal, so I'll request a
480p draft.

00:08:04.880 --> 00:08:10.060
I ask for a 15 second widescreen draft at
480p using my photo.

00:08:10.060 --> 00:08:11.840
Then I click the send arrow.

00:08:11.840 --> 00:08:15.440
Check the settings and price, then click
approve to generate.

00:08:15.440 --> 00:08:18.340
Pause here and choose a moment you want to
see on screen.

00:08:18.340 --> 00:08:20.300
Describe it in three sentences.

00:08:20.300 --> 00:08:23.520
Who is there, where they are and what
happens.

00:08:23.520 --> 00:08:27.420
Use one person and one location for this
exercise.

00:08:27.420 --> 00:08:29.920
Attach your photo if you want to be in it.

00:08:29.920 --> 00:08:34.100
Ask for the interview, answer the
questions, then read the prompt.

00:08:34.100 --> 00:08:38.020
Request one 15 second widescreen draft at
480p.

00:08:38.020 --> 00:08:40.600
Two drafts is the limit for this exercise.

00:08:40.600 --> 00:08:44.390
Come back when your video is ready.

00:08:44.400 --> 00:08:48.160
Mine's ready. Click the video thumbnail
and play it from the beginning.

00:08:48.160 --> 00:08:49.160
Let's

00:08:50.720 --> 00:08:51.720
watch.

00:09:04.060 --> 00:09:08.900
You can see how quickly an idea becomes
something you can actually watch.

00:09:08.900 --> 00:09:13.260
We just took a scene from my imagination
and brought it to the screen.

00:09:13.260 --> 00:09:18.580
Right here. I like the warm bar and the
quiet mood, but we see the

00:09:18.580 --> 00:09:20.180
window before I get there.

00:09:20.180 --> 00:09:22.000
I want to save that for the end.

00:09:22.000 --> 00:09:25.200
If a scene needs one note, I don't fire
the whole crew.

00:09:25.200 --> 00:09:27.240
I just tell it what I want changed.

00:09:27.240 --> 00:09:29.880
I write the note you see here.

00:09:29.880 --> 00:09:34.140
Keep the window outside the opening frame
and reveal earth at the end.

00:09:34.140 --> 00:09:39.090
Keep the person, bar, action and mood the
same and rewrite the prompt before

00:09:39.200 --> 00:09:44.340
generating. Then I click the send arrow
right here in the same chat.

00:09:44.340 --> 00:09:48.640
He gives me a new prompt but adds curtains
to the bar.

00:09:48.640 --> 00:09:52.100
That's not the change I asked for, so I
correct him again.

00:09:52.100 --> 00:09:54.620
I'm still only changing the text.

00:09:54.620 --> 00:09:57.480
A few moments later, he gives me another
prompt.

00:09:57.480 --> 00:10:01.920
I read through it, check that the changes
match my idea and start the

00:10:01.920 --> 00:10:04.240
generation. Here's the new version.

00:10:04.240 --> 00:10:08.330
Click the thumbnail and let's watch.

00:10:21.880 --> 00:10:26.000
Now, compare that moment. Does the window
appear when I wanted it to?

00:10:26.000 --> 00:10:29.240
That's what I'm checking. The idea is
still mine.

00:10:29.240 --> 00:10:33.990
I gave it feedback in ordinary language
and it made another version.

00:10:36.660 --> 00:10:40.300
That's the loop. Idea prompt result tweak.

00:10:40.300 --> 00:10:43.560
After a take, choose one important change
for the next draft.

00:10:43.560 --> 00:10:47.540
Stay in the same chat. Pause and watch
your video all the way through.

00:10:47.540 --> 00:10:51.180
Compare the person, place and main action
with your idea.

00:10:51.180 --> 00:10:53.320
Then check the moment you cared about
most.

00:10:53.320 --> 00:10:54.920
Did it happen the way you wanted?

00:10:54.920 --> 00:10:58.800
If something needs fixing, describe the
change in ordinary language.

00:10:58.800 --> 00:11:02.740
Read the updated prompt, then generate
another version if you need it.

00:11:02.740 --> 00:11:06.820
Keep a take that works, stop after at most
two drafts.

00:11:06.820 --> 00:11:10.080
Save the version you prefer, note anything
unfinished and come

00:11:10.080 --> 00:11:14.080
back. Look at what we started with.

00:11:14.080 --> 00:11:18.020
One paragraph about my job and three
sentences I could have texted to a

00:11:18.020 --> 00:11:22.620
friend. Now, I have a research shortlist
and a draft of that scene.

00:11:22.620 --> 00:11:28.050
Something I can use and something I wanted
to see.

00:11:28.120 --> 00:11:33.060
Your homework is to use your second brain
for one real task and create a 15

00:11:33.060 --> 00:11:35.420
second scene from your own idea.

00:11:35.420 --> 00:11:38.620
If you follow the pauses, you've already
started.

00:11:38.620 --> 00:11:40.780
Now finish and save your work.

00:11:40.780 --> 00:11:45.380
Keep the useful answer and your chosen
video with the idea and prompt that

00:11:45.380 --> 00:11:50.790
made it. Add two short notes, what you
asked for and what you kept

00:11:50.840 --> 00:11:55.740
or changed and why. Next lesson, you'll
learn to create content and ads for

00:11:55.740 --> 00:12:00.680
any business in minutes. Product photos,
social posts, a video

00:12:00.680 --> 00:12:04.320
ad, all starting with a photo of one
ordinary object.

00:12:04.320 --> 00:12:08.550
So bring one thing you own, a bottle, a
mug or a pair of shoes

00:12:09.780 --> 00:12:10.780
and stay tuned.
